Rename apv_parser.c's static `close()` so it can no longer hijack libc
`close()` in full-LTO builds on macOS/arm64.

On Darwin clang gives every *external* C symbol an ELF-style asm label, so
`close()` declared in <unistd.h> reaches the IR as `@"\01_close"`, while a
`static` function keeps the plain IR name `@close`. LLVM's LTO resolver keeps
those two apart, but after resolution both map onto the same flat Mach-O
symbol name `_close` in the single merged codegen unit, so libavformat's
`file_close()` (libavformat/file.c) calls this AVBSF callback with the raw
file descriptor instead of libc:

    00000001007694e4 <_file_close>:
      ldr x8, [x0, #0x10]     ; h->priv_data
      ldr w0, [x8, #0x8]      ; c->fd
      bl  0x101c386c8 <_close> ; not libc close()

    0000000101c386c8 <_close>:
      ldr x19, [x0]           ; p = s->priv_data   <-- x0 == fd (3)

so every avformat_close_input()/avio_close() of a "file:" URL dereferences the
fd and dies with EXC_BAD_ACCESS, i.e. ffprobe/ffmpeg segfault as soon as they
close an input file.

This is the same defect reported in
https://trac.ffmpeg.org/ticket/11479 ("Segfault with LTO - MacOS M4"), which
was bisected to e504247db6edb1cb47a9c562277f6e671f4bde1d. That commit added
the identical `static void close()` to libavcodec/ffv1_parser.c, and upstream
later renamed that one to `ffv1_close`; the APV parser has since reintroduced
the exact same pattern, so rename it here too.

Only the -flto (full LTO) code path is affected. -flto=thin and non-LTO builds
code-generate each translation unit separately and stay correct, as do
non-Darwin targets, where no `\01` asm label is involved.

Upstream: https://trac.ffmpeg.org/ticket/11479
Context:  https://ffmpeg.org/doxygen/8.0/file_002c_002avformat_002file_002ec-source.html

diff --git a/libavcodec/apv_parser.c b/libavcodec/apv_parser.c
index 3417bd751fdb..f81b3b8a8977 100644
--- a/libavcodec/apv_parser.c
+++ b/libavcodec/apv_parser.c
@@ -194,7 +194,7 @@ static av_cold int init(AVCodecParserContext *s)
     return 0;
 }
 
-static av_cold void close(AVCodecParserContext *s)
+static av_cold void apv_close(AVCodecParserContext *s)
 {
     APVParseContext *p = s->priv_data;
     ParseContext *pc = &p->pc;
@@ -209,5 +209,5 @@ static av_cold void close(AVCodecParserContext *s)
     .priv_data_size = sizeof(APVParseContext),
     .init           = init,
     .parse          = parse,
-    .close          = close,
+    .close          = apv_close,
 };